  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-26T17:25:49.313Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's clear that build 1299 changed the way disconnects were handled. But I feel they are being handled incorrectly.\n\nI am getting disconnected more frequently. And every time I'm stuck at a prompt until I interact with it, and then after I click, \"Retry\" I am forced back to my home world. \n\nIt feels the behavior of disconnects should be:\n\n1. It should appear that you are disconnected the immediate that it's detected, but should attempt reconnecting.\n\n2. If a reload of the world must occur, then the user should be reloaded in place (Return the user to the position and orientation they were after reconnecting)\n\n3. Returning to Home should be an option, never forced.",
